---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import { settings } from '../lib/site';
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Mark from '../assets/identity/mark.svg';
import Mark16 from '../assets/identity/mark-16.svg';
import LockupH from '../assets/identity/lockup-horizontal.svg';
import LockupS from '../assets/identity/lockup-stacked.svg';
import inUse from '../assets/identity/in-use.png';

const manifesto = settings.manifesto.split(/\n\s*\n/).map((p) => p.trim()).filter(Boolean);

// The tools Daniel moved through, in order, on the way to building with AI.
const tools = ['Google AI Studio', 'Google Jules', 'Cursor', 'Google Antigravity', 'Lovable', 'ChatGPT', 'Claude Code'];
---
<Base title="About" description="inside a head is a personal studio for tech experiments and aesthetic design. Ideas are messy; this is where they get built.">
  <article class="wrap about">
    <header class="manifesto grid">
      <h1>{settings.manifestoTitle}</h1>
      <div class="manifesto-text">
        {manifesto.map((p, i) => (i === manifesto.length - 1 ? <p class="closing">{p}</p> : <p>{p}</p>))}
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="studio-title">
      <h2 id="studio-title">The studio</h2>
      <div class="text lead-text">
        <p>
          It’s a coffee shop that’s open past midnight. It smells of coffee, there’s some music playing in the
          background, and you can really chill and think. There are a lot of books, because each book is an idea, a
          project that hasn’t started yet. It’s messy, it’s quiet, and it’s a life worth living.
        </p>
        <p>
          Think of the quiet planets in <cite>Cowboy Bebop</cite> (the anime, not the TV series): small, safe and far
          from the noise. It smells of coffee and plays jazz. Stay as long as you like.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="me-title">
      <h2 id="me-title">Daniel</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          It’s complicated. I’ve always liked exploring and learning new things, and that’s what I’m doing now:
          exploring, and building the things I like. I drive for Uber and Bolt to keep things going, and this is where
          I keep my creative side alive.
        </p>
        <p>
          I was a shy kid, more the second guy than the first. But I was always curious.
        </p>
        <p>
          Why <em>inside a head</em>? Because I always live in my head. I think about things, build scenarios, come up
          with ideas about everything and critique everything, all in there. This is me, always thinking.
        </p>
        <p>
          Music came first. One of the first things I did with a phone was look for a way to listen to music with the
          screen off. That’s how I found Spotify, and, being broke and without a subscription, how I found APKs and
          cracked APKs. That’s where some of my love for tech comes from. I picked up the guitar in ninth or tenth
          grade, and my teacher told me I’d never be able to play because I wasn’t talented. Somehow I did, and I play
          decently well now. I became a musician by working hard and surrounding myself with better musicians.
        </p>
        <p>I’m an idealist and a dreamer. The builder and the musician I’ve had to earn.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="pm-title">
      <h2 id="pm-title">Product</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          I didn’t plan it. A friend called about an open role where he worked and said he thought I’d like it. I did.
          Not necessarily that job, but the idea of product management: being the one who makes the calls about the
          product, talking with developers and customers, brainstorming solutions.
        </p>
        <p>
          I worked on workforce management software. The hardest part was being thrown in as a junior in the middle of
          a cloud transformation, with no corporate experience, talking to some of the most important people in the
          company and somehow making them believe me.
        </p>
        <p>
          What I’m proudest of is helping others, and the day a boss finally acknowledged that what I’d been saying was
          true and important. What I got wrong taught me that you need more courage to stand your ground, and that you
          need to prepare better.
        </p>
        <p class="pull">A good PM prepares, and understands the product.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="build-title">
      <h2 id="build-title">How I build</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          I started after a job interview. The person I talked to showed me what was possible, and curiosity took over.
        </p>
        <ol class="journey mono" aria-label="Tools, in the order I used them">
          {tools.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
        </ol>
        <p>
          The AI writes the code. I still do the discovery: talking with customers and checking whether there’s a gap
          in the market. And I like to build the framework first: why I’m doing this, how, and for whom.
        </p>
        <p>
          It isn’t “ask, and the AI does it”. It needs direction, and I believe that direction is the difference
          between slop and products that can grow.
        </p>
        <dl class="facts-list">
          <div><dt class="mono">Every day</dt><dd>Claude Code and Obsidian. Surprisingly, Instagram and Threads too, to keep up with the market.</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="mono">Learning now</dt><dd>Marketing, and how to take a product to market.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <h2 id="next-title">Where I’m headed</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          A small, decent start-up that brings in 2,000–3,000 a month after taxes, with room to grow. And maybe, one
          day, a physical space of my own: a coffee shop, or something like it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <h2 id="work-title">If you’re here about work</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          I’m a product manager with around four years in enterprise SaaS, open to remote product roles, junior to mid
          level.
        </p>
        <p class="links">
          <a href="/resume">Resume</a>
          <a href={settings.linkedin} rel="me noreferrer">LinkedIn <Arrow /></a>
          <a href={settings.github} rel="me noreferrer">GitHub <Arrow /></a>
          <a href={`mailto:${settings.email}`}>Email</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="design-title">
      <h2 id="design-title">Design</h2>
      <div class="text">
        <p>
          The mark is a square head with the idea sitting inside it, off-centre, where a thought would be. Two shapes
          on one grid, nothing else: structure, with a little mess inside. The name is always lowercase.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="kit">
        <figure class="panel paper wide">
          <LockupH class="lockup-h" role="img" aria-label="inside a head logo" />
          <figcaption class="mono">Primary lockup</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="panel ink">
          <Mark class="mark-big" role="img" aria-label="inside a head mark, reversed" />
          <figcaption class="mono">Mark, reversed</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="panel paper">
          <LockupS class="lockup-s" role="img" aria-label="inside a head stacked logo" />
          <figcaption class="mono">Stacked lockup</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="panel paper">
          <div class="ladder">
            <Mark style="width: 64px; height: 64px" aria-hidden="true" />
            <Mark style="width: 32px; height: 32px" aria-hidden="true" />
            <Mark16 style="width: 16px; height: 16px" aria-hidden="true" />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="mono">64 · 32 · 16 px, with a pixel-snapped cut for 16</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <dl class="spec">
        <div>
          <dt class="mono">Colour</dt>
          <dd class="swatches">
            <span><i class="chip" style="background: #0b0b0a"></i>Ink <span class="mono">#0B0B0A</span></span>
            <span><i class="chip" style="background: #f4f3ef"></i>Paper <span class="mono">#F4F3EF</span></span>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="mono">Type</dt>
          <dd><span class="specimen">Geist</span> <span class="specimen mono-face">Geist Mono</span></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="mono">Grid</dt>
          <dd>12 columns, 4 on phones. Colour belongs to the projects.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <figure class="in-use">
        <Picture src={inUse} alt="The logo in use: on a website header, a browser tab, an app icon, business cards, a social profile and a laptop sticker." formats={['webp']} widths={[800, 1400, 2304]} sizes="(min-width: 960px) 90vw, 100vw" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption class="mono">In use</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p class="colophon">
        Built with Astro and Keystatic, written in plain Markdown, in the open, on{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/iDarcky/Inside-a-Head" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { padding-bottom: var(--s-16); }
  .manifesto { padding-block: var(--s-12) var(--s-24); row-gap: var(--s-12); }
  h1 {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 1rem + 10vw, 11rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    line-height: 0.86;
    max-width: 8ch;
    margin-left: -0.04em;
  }
  .manifesto-text {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-6);
    font-size: var(--t-lead);
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    max-width: 40ch;
  }
  .closing { font-weight: 600; }
  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .manifesto-text { grid-column: 6 / span 7; }
  }

  .block { border-top: 2px solid var(--rule); padding-block: var(--s-3) var(--s-16); row-gap: var(--s-6); }
  .block h2 { grid-column: 1 / -1; font-size: var(--t-h3); letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1; }
  .text { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .block h2 { grid-column: 1 / span 4; }
    .text { grid-column: 6 / span 7; }
  }
  .text { display: grid; gap: var(--s-4); max-width: 62ch; font-size: 1.125rem; }
  .muted { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s-2) var(--s-6); font-size: var(--t-small); }
  .links a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-1); }

  .lead-text { font-size: var(--t-lead); line-height: 1.35; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  cite { font-style: italic; }
  .pull { font-size: var(--t-lead); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.25; }
  .journey {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--s-2) var(--s-3);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .journey li:not(:last-child)::after { content: '→'; margin-left: var(--s-3); }
  .journey li:last-child { color: var(--ink); }
  .facts-list { display: grid; gap: var(--s-3); margin-top: var(--s-2); }
  .facts-list div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr; gap: var(--s-4); align-items: baseline; }
  .facts-list dt { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .work .text { border: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding: var(--s-6); }

  .kit, .spec, .in-use, .colophon { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .kit {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--gutter);
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .kit { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    .kit .wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  }
  .panel {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--s-6);
    min-height: 260px;
    padding: var(--s-8) var(--s-6) var(--s-4);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--hairline);
  }
  .panel > :global(svg) { align-self: center; justify-self: center; }
  /* Fixed colours: these panels show the logo as it is, whatever the site theme. */
  .panel.paper { background: #f4f3ef; color: #0b0b0a; }
  .panel.ink { background: #0b0b0a; color: #f4f3ef; }
  .panel figcaption { opacity: 0.7; }
  .wide { min-height: 320px; }
  .lockup-h { width: min(100%, 560px); height: auto; }
  .lockup-s { width: min(80%, 260px); height: auto; }
  .mark-big { width: 112px; height: 112px; }
  .ladder { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: center; gap: var(--s-8); align-self: center; }

  .spec { display: grid; gap: var(--s-4); margin-top: var(--s-12); max-width: 62ch; }
  .spec div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 5rem 1fr; gap: var(--s-4); align-items: baseline; }
  .spec dt { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .swatches { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s-6); }
  .swatches > span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-2); }
  .swatches .mono { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .chip { display: inline-block; width: 20px; height: 20px; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--hairline); }
  .specimen { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-right: var(--s-6); }
  .mono-face { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0; font-size: 1.25rem; }

  .in-use { margin-top: var(--s-12); }
  .in-use :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .in-use figcaption { color: var(--ink-2); margin-top: var(--s-3); }
  .colophon { margin-top: var(--s-12); color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 62ch; }
  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .spec, .colophon { grid-column: 6 / span 7; }
  }
</style>
